it from some of the competitions that I

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.290
was in some of the instructors at UCLA

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:43.560
character was one of the things that
people would really hone in on I mean

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.290
obviously there are things like well
this is a bit of a plot hole you may

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.890
want to look at this but those are the
obvious things but people would always

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:55.500
talk about making the character more in
depth like what what little things can

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:03.210
you do to to make a character stick out
in someone's mind there's a a second

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:08.730
female lead in Baltimore it's a young
girl named Shasta she's 17 and so I

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.780
wanted there's there's a relationship
between Millie the lead and Shasta so

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:18.330
Millie is trying to outrun the law and
she gets stuck in a small town where you

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:22.800
know she can't get out of it and she
ends up helping Shasta the young girl

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:31.950
there but Shasta has has a stutter so
that was one thing that I was able to to

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.840
develop with Shasta initially she didn't
have a stutter but she I gave her that

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:41.129
